messages.content:
You rewrite short texts that are READ ALOUD to a child in grade 3-5 after they answer a quiz question.
HARD LIMIT: each text becomes ONE or TWO short sentences, of AT MOST 18 words (count them: "max_words" below). Over the limit is wrong. Write in English. Keep only the ONE idea that tells the child why; cut everything else (no "as we saw", no "remember that", no restating the question).
Everyday words a child of that age uses at home. No clause inside a clause, no "which"/"that is"/"whereas" chains, no passive voice. Speak to the child directly when you speak to them, with no gender ("you").
KEEP THE MEANING EXACTLY: the same reason, the same right answer, every number it gave. A text for a wrong option still says why that option is not right (never praise it). Do not add a new fact. Do not mention the teacher or "the lesson". Simpler must still be TRUE: never trade accuracy for brevity ("was cleaning" is the past, never "happening now").
Example (grade 1-2, max 12): "In a subtraction problem, the bigger number is the one you start with before taking anything away." → "You start with the bigger number."
Return JSON only: { "texts": [ { "id": 0, "text": "" } ] } — one entry per id below, in any order.

{"id":0,"question":"Which of these is a proper fraction?","right_answer":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","kind":"explanation","text":"A proper fraction has a top number smaller than the bottom number. In $\\frac{2}{5}$, 2 is smaller than 5.","words_now":19,"max_words":18}
{"id":1,"question":"What is the improper fraction $\\frac{7}{4}$ written as a Mixed Number?","right_answer":"$1\\frac{3}{4}$","kind":"explanation","text":"Divide the top number by the bottom number. The answer is the whole number, the leftover is the new top number.","words_now":21,"max_words":18}
{"id":2,"question":"What is the improper fraction $\\frac{7}{4}$ written as a Mixed Number?","right_answer":"$1\\frac{3}{4}$","kind":"correct","text":"Yes! $\\frac{7}{4}$ means 7 divided by 4. That is 1 whole with 3 left over, so $1\\frac{3}{4}$.","words_now":17,"max_words":18}
{"id":3,"question":"What is the improper fraction $\\frac{7}{4}$ written as a Mixed Number?","right_answer":"$1\\frac{3}{4}$","feedback_for_wrong_option":"$1\\frac{1}{4}$","kind":"wrong","text":"When you divide 7 by 4, you get 1 whole. There are 3 parts left over, so the fraction is $\\frac{3}{4}$.","words_now":21,"max_words":18}
{"id":4,"question":"What is the improper fraction $\\frac{9}{5}$ written as a Mixed Number?","right_answer":"$1\\frac{4}{5}$","kind":"explanation","text":"Divide the top number by the bottom number. The answer is the whole number, the leftover is the new top number.","words_now":21,"max_words":18}
{"id":5,"question":"What is the improper fraction $\\frac{9}{5}$ written as a Mixed Number?","right_answer":"$1\\frac{4}{5}$","kind":"correct","text":"Excellent! When you divide 9 by 5, you get 1 with a remainder of 4, so it is $1\\frac{4}{5}$.","words_now":19,"max_words":18}
